_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":1355.888888888889,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":349.8888888888889,"requests":1},"T6":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":1717.625,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":254.25,"requests":1},"T9":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":1717.625,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":254.25,"requests":1},"necessity":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":1717.625,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":254.25,"requests":1},"prerequisite-consistency":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":9778.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":110.0,"requests":1},"project.portability":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":1717.625,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":254.25,"requests":1},"project.symbol-reference-completeness":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":218835.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":4975.0,"requests":7}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define the source/computation of `effective_excluded_sync_types` (per-project axis vs derived from type_map SKIP vs override of EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES) and how it composes with the SKIP decision.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.07,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Scope lists 'effective_excluded_sync_types' as a new config.py function without defining its inputs/axis","Finding 1 says syncable = 'get_args(TicketType) − EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES, minus the effective excluded set' — two distinct exclusion sources named but their relationship/provenance not defined","Census: 'Per-project excluded set replaces the single EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES read (:377) at BOTH consumers' without stating how the per-project set is computed"],"finding":"`config.effective_excluded_sync_types` is named as a new Scope deliverable and referenced ('minus the effective excluded set', 'per-project excluded set replaces the single EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES read'), but its SOURCE/computation is under-specified: it is unclear whether the per-project excluded set derives from SKIP entries in the effective type_map, from a separate config axis, or from a per-project override of EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb982fc475bbbfcc0","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope (effective_excluded_sync_types); Finding 1; census 'Per-project excluded set replaces the single EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES read'","norm_id":"n448b9d65b9fbfa82","priority":0.67,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor must decide whether SKIP and the excluded set are the same mechanism or two axes"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State in Finding 1 whether the per-project excluded set is a distinct config axis or is computed from SKIP-valued type_map entries, and give its default (= EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES when no project override).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Reconcile Finding 2 with the create data-flow (mapper sets issuetype; dispatch_one:188-195 derives ticket_type from it): either resolve the type at the mapper layer only (as DC's _issues.py already does) and drop acli's capitalize passthrough without adding a second local->Jira mapping, or specify exactly how acli distinguishes an already-mapped Jira name from an unmapped local type and where the effective type_map is written onto the create payload.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.08,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["outbound_fields.py:143 result['issuetype'] = _LOCAL_TO_JIRA_TYPE.get(ticket.get('ticket_type','task'),'Task') — mapper emits the Jira type name","dispatch_one.py:188-195 derives _ticket_data['ticket_type'] from _ticket_data.get('issuetype') (the already-mapped Jira name), defaulting 'Task'","acli.py:282 issue_type = ticket_data.get('ticket_type','Task').capitalize() — on the differ path ticket_type is already a Jira name","jira_datacenter/_issues.py:188 consumes the pre-mapped issuetype directly via _translate_create_fields and never re-maps ticket_type — proving acli is the anomaly","Finding 2 claims 'an unknown syncable type (\"spike\") is capitalized through, never coerced to Task' — true only for a non-differ direct caller, not the compute_outbound_mutations path the epic targets"],"finding":"Finding 2's acli fix is at odds with the real create data-flow: on the differ path acli.create_issue never receives a raw local type. The mapper (_map_local_to_jira_fields:143 / DC backend:86) already sets issuetype to the mapped Jira name, and dispatch_one:188-195 derives ticket_data['ticket_type'] FROM that already-mapped issuetype. Making acli re-resolve ticket_type through the local->Jira type map and fail-close on undecided would fail-close on EVERY differ create (a Jira name like 'Story' is not a key of LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA) — a double-mapping / wrong-layer defect.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5b8f01bf85ff3e17","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach > Finding 2 (acli.py:282 rewrite); AC test_acli_create_issue_maps_and_fails_closed","norm_id":"n719e12b356789a6d","priority":0.68,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Any differ-driven create through the Cloud/acli transport: acli receives issuetype-derived ticket_type ('Story','Task') and, under the plan's fix, tries to map it as if it were a local key","A type_map that remaps local 'bug'->'Story': acli receives 'Story' and fail-closes because 'Story' is not a LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA key"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Prefer resolving issue type solely in the mapper (Finding 4) and make acli consume the mapper-produced issuetype like the DC transport does (_issues.py:188), replacing acli.py:282's capitalize with a pass-through of the resolved issuetype; if a transport-level guard is still wanted, have acli fail-closed ONLY when issuetype is absent, not re-map ticket_type through the local->Jira map.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify explicitly how the effective type map (or the resolved issuetype) reaches acli.create_issue: name the builder site that stamps it onto create_fields (analogous to _BRIDGE_TARGET_PROJECT_KEY at outbound_mutation_builders.py:124) and confirm dispatch_one preserves it, OR drop the acli-side map in favor of the mapper-resolved issuetype.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Finding 4 wiring: '_compute_outbound_create_mutation passes type_map=' — i.e. to the mapper call, not onto create_fields","outbound_mutation_builders.py:124 create_fields[_BRIDGE_TARGET_PROJECT_KEY] = canonical is the only payload stamp described; no analogous type-map stamp is specified","dispatch_one.py:182-183 passes mutation['fields'] through verbatim (dict copy), so any type map would have to be stamped onto create_fields to reach acli"],"finding":"Finding 2 says the effective type map is 'carried on the create payload beside _bridge_target_project', but the plan never states where that map is written onto create_fields. Finding 4's builder wiring only forwards type_map INTO the mapper (map_local_to_remote), not onto the payload dict, and _bridge_target_project is stamped as a scalar string in _compute_outbound_create_mutation:124 — leaving the acli-visible type map unpopulated.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"febcd14b351a5b01a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach > Finding 2 and Finding 4; outbound_mutation_builders.py:124","norm_id":"na61141609afcfbd4","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["acli.create_issue tries to read the effective type map from ticket_data but the builder never stamped it → falls back to a default/empty map"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a test that a non-lossy type (forward target reverses cleanly via config.jira_to_local_type) is NOT stamped with rebar-type: and still round-trips inbound with no label present.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.075,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Finding 3: '_desired_type_annotation stamps only when the forward target does NOT reverse to this local type'","AC lists the stamp-when-lossy case and recover case but no explicit no-stamp-when-lossless assertion — absence rationale: the decision branch has two outcomes and only one is covered."],"finding":"The new _desired_type_annotation stamp rule is a conditional (stamp ONLY when the forward target does not reverse to this local type), but the AC tests exercise only the stamp branch (test_rebar_type_label_stamped_when_lossy). There is no named test for the non-lossy branch — a type whose forward target reverses cleanly must NOT be stamped (and inbound must recover correctly with no label present).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff9029d16c313e6ab","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — test_rebar_type_label_stamped_when_lossy / test_rebar_type_label_recovered_reverse_map_free","norm_id":"nddf6621c6dcd4251","priority":0.875,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add test_rebar_type_label_absent_when_lossless asserting _diff_type_annotation_labels produces no stamp when config.jira_to_local_type[target] == local_type, and recover_type_label falls back to the raw type when no rebar-type: label exists.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend Finding 2 (and its AC) to also rewrite the DC transport's create path jira_datacenter/_issues.py:79 `_create_issuetype` to resolve issuetype via the effective type map and fail closed on undecided types, mirroring the acli.py:282 fix.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'adapters/jira/acli.py:282 (JiraClient.create_issue, the transport's OWN method ...) computes issue_type = ticket_data.get(\"ticket_type\",\"Task\").capitalize() ... an unknown syncable type (\"spike\") is capitalized through, never coerced to Task. FIX ... resolve issue_type via the effective type map ... fail-closed on undecided type.'","jira_datacenter/_issues.py:88-90: `bridge_type = ticket_data.get('ticket_type'); if isinstance(bridge_type, str) and bridge_type.strip(): return {'name': bridge_type.strip().capitalize()}` — same capitalize passthrough, no type-map, default {'name':'Task'} at :99","jira_datacenter/_issues.py:84 docstring: '(a bridge-side string such as \"task\", capitalized the way Cloud's AcliClient.create_issue capitalizes it)'","jira_datacenter/_issues.py:120: 'CREATE is a SECOND DC send path, distinct from the update path's mapper' — the mapper-path fix in Finding 4 does not reach it","dispatch_one.py:188-195 derives ticket_type from issuetype and hands it to client.create_issue for both transports"],"finding":"Finding 2 inventories the transport-level ticket_type capitalize-passthrough at only Cloud's JiraClient.create_issue (acli.py:282) and omits the DC transport's parallel create path _create_issuetype (jira_datacenter/_issues.py:79). That function does the identical `ticket_data.get('ticket_type').capitalize()` with a 'Task' default and no type-map; its own docstring says it capitalizes 'the way Cloud's AcliClient.create_issue capitalizes it', and _issues.py:120 calls CREATE 'a SECOND DC send path, distinct from the update path's mapper' — so Finding 4's mapper fix (_map_local_to_dc_fields) does not cover it. dispatch_one.py:188-195 feeds ticket_type into client.create_issue on both transports, so DC recapitalizes unknown syncable types exactly as Cloud does.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f15e0487ac660e2c4","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Finding 2 (G1G2/G6) — 'acli.py:282 needs a MATERIALLY DIFFERENT rewrite'; Scope line 'acli.py:282'","norm_id":"n890ca8ca4fe8ffe5","priority":0.8,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["jira_datacenter/_issues.py:79 _create_issuetype — on a DC deployment an undecided syncable type (e.g. 'spike') is silently capitalized to 'Spike' instead of failing closed, defeating the parent AC's fail-closed guarantee on the DC transport","The AC test_acli_create_issue_maps_and_fails_closed exercises only the Cloud transport; DC's _create_issuetype has no analogous mapping/fail-closed and would ship the pre-existing passthrough unchanged"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add jira_datacenter/_issues.py `_create_issuetype` (called from _translate_create_fields:117 / create_issue:165) to Finding 2's inventory and Scope, applying the same type-map resolution + fail-closed treatment as acli.py:282; extend test_acli_create_issue_maps_and_fails_closed (or add a DC sibling) to cover both transports.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Either add a covering criterion for the per-project excluded-set override, or clarify that SKIP is the sole exclusion mechanism and drop the separate `effective_excluded_sync_types` framing.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5375,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Scope names 'effective_excluded_sync_types' as a new function","AC list has test_type_skip_excludes_ticket_both_consumers (SKIP) but no criterion naming the per-project excluded-set override as a separate outcome"],"finding":"The plan introduces a `effective_excluded_sync_types` / per-project excluded set as a deliverable but no acceptance criterion exclusively covers it distinct from the SKIP path; `test_type_skip_excludes_ticket_both_consumers` tests SKIP-driven exclusion, leaving the per-project excluded-set override potentially uncovered.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f693b5cc4e2ea64bb","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria; Scope (effective_excluded_sync_types)","norm_id":"n51da7ad591eeee60","priority":0.4125,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A project that overrides EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES (if that is a separate axis) has no proving test"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Document the migration/rollout for the fail-closed cutover (e.g. builtin type_map covers the known {bug,story,task,epic} so only genuinely-new types fail) and note the back-out path.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.601,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Finding 2: 'an unknown syncable type (\"spike\") is capitalized through, never coerced to Task. FIX: ... fail-closed on undecided type'","Finding 1: gate 'fires ONCE UP-FRONT, before the mutation loop' raising MappingConfigError","No migration note for existing projects whose configs lack decisions for currently-syncable types"],"finding":"Replacing the create-site capitalize-passthrough with fail-closed changes existing behavior: syncable types not yet decided in a project's config (previously silently coerced/capitalized) will now raise MappingConfigError at compute_outbound_mutations. This is an operational breaking change for existing projects with no stated migration/rollout or back-out note.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd706682f016e4561","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Finding 1 (up-front fail-closed gate); Finding 2 (acli.py:282 fail-closed)","norm_id":"n78116a785187dfe2","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An existing project syncing a type absent from LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA and not in config now hard-fails at load where it previously synced"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a note that the builtin MappingLayer(type_map=LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA) keeps the four known types decided by default, so only projects with additional syncable types must add decisions; state that reverting is config-only.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the `TicketType` source to `rebar.types` (parent package, `src/rebar/types.py:23`, NOT a `rebar_reconciler` sibling) and specify HOW each new `get_args(TicketType)` consumer imports it — respecting config.py's stdlib-only-at-import-time constraint (e.g. a lazy function-local import, as mapping_config.py:213 / runtime.py:230 already do for `from rebar import ...`).","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.48,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["search for `TicketType` under src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler returned (no matches)","src/rebar/types.py:23: `TicketType = Literal[\"bug\", \"epic\", \"story\", \"task\", \"session_log\", \"code_review\", \"identity\"]` — under the `rebar` package","config.py header comment: 'this module imports nothing but __future__' / 'operator-overridable status literals above must never sit behind an adapter/config import' — a stdlib-only-at-import-time constraint the new gate must respect","existing inbound_fields._LOCAL_STATUS_VOCAB (:149) derives from `_JIRA_TO_LOCAL_STATUS.values()`, NOT from `TicketType` — the codebase currently avoids importing TicketType into the reconciler","reconciler `from rebar import ...` usages (mapping_config.py:213, runtime.py:230) are function-local/lazy, establishing the pattern any new rebar.* dependency would need to follow"],"finding":"The plan cites `get_args(TicketType)` at `types.py:23`, but `TicketType` is not a `rebar_reconciler` module symbol — it is defined in the PARENT package at `src/rebar/types.py:23`. The plan mislocates it as a sibling reconciler module and never names the cross-package import source for the three NEW `get_args(TicketType)` consumers it adds.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff035fc41c263d39f","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Finding 1 (config.assert_type_decisions_complete / effective_excluded_sync_types) and Surface-parity census (inbound_fields._LOCAL_TYPE_VOCAB); Context line 'get_args(TicketType) (`types.py:23`)'","norm_id":"nf44d4996ba8309ae","priority":0.22,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer adds a top-level `from rebar.types import TicketType` to config.py, violating its stdlib-only-at-import-time invariant","Implementer cannot find `TicketType` in a `rebar_reconciler.types` module (which does not exist) and stalls or fabricates a local literal that then drifts from the canonical Literal"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"In config.assert_type_decisions_complete / effective_excluded_sync_types, import TicketType lazily inside the function (`from rebar.types import TicketType`), mirroring the lazy `from rebar_reconciler import mapping_config` pattern in effective_status_map, so config.py stays stdlib-only at module import time; for inbound_fields._LOCAL_TYPE_VOCAB, either import lazily or derive from the parity-tested reverse map value